            <p class="text-sm font-semibold mt-4">Even on Slow&nbsp;3G (~500 kbps + 2&nbsp;s RTT), the dynamic intersection stayed at ~1&nbsp;fps with every frame sharp and plates readable; the static scene rode every tier at 1 fps or below because the codec emits almost nothing when nothing changes.</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-2 leading-relaxed">Method: <code>performance_start_trace</code> over each (camera, tier) for 60&nbsp;s after a 30&nbsp;s settle; bytes/fps parsed from raw WebSocket events. Chrome's named throttle presets approximate the playbook's idealized caps. <strong>Synthetic throttle &ne; real cellular</strong> &mdash; real LTE/5G adds jitter and burstiness this method cannot reproduce. iOS and Android native-app sweeps measured similarly at tier A (both delivered ~2&nbsp;fps at the 256&nbsp;kbps cap); see <a href="/docs/benchmarks/03-remote-viewing-methodology" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">full methodology</a> for the per-platform breakdown.</p>
