          <!-- Bundle 05 — live-stream uplink (FDC vs direct RTSP)    -->
          <!-- ====================================================== -->
          <div id="live-bandwidth" class="mt-8 bg-white border border-blue-200 rounded-lg p-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold text-blue-700 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Measured uplink</p>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-xl mb-1">What live remote viewing costs the trailer's LTE/5G uplink
              <span class="text-sm font-normal text-gray-600">(<time datetime="2026-05-22">May 2026</time>, one Puget Sound camera, 2688&times;1520)</span></h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">Sequential A-B-A-B captures at the camera's native resolution &mdash; same scene window, two delivery paths, wire bytes measured per consumer process.</p>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
              <caption class="sr-only">Live-stream uplink kbps and GB/24h for direct RTSP vs FDC-over-NVR</caption>
              <thead><tr class="border-b bg-gray-50">
                <th class="py-2 px-2">Delivery path</th>
                <th class="py-2 px-2">Mean kbps</th>
                <th class="py-2 px-2">GB / cam / 24h</th>
                <th class="py-2 px-2">Sample range</th>
              </tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr class="border-b"><td class="py-2 px-2">Direct camera RTSP (H.264)</td><td class="py-2 px-2">2,626</td><td class="py-2 px-2">28.4</td><td class="py-2 px-2">&plusmn;0.4% across N=2</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="py-2 px-2">FDC live via NVR <a class="text-blue-600 hover:underline" href="#fdc-codec">(see codec)</a></td><td class="py-2 px-2">1,425</td><td class="py-2 px-2">15.4</td><td class="py-2 px-2">&plusmn;19.2% across N=2</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold mt-4">FDC delivery saved <strong>~46% of uplink bytes</strong> vs direct RTSP for the same scene &mdash; about 13&nbsp;GB / camera / day off the cellular link.</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-3 leading-relaxed">Method: two 120-second samples per path interleaved A-B-A-B, with per-process wire bytes measured via <code>nettop</code>. Both <code>range_pct_of_mean</code> figures fell within the bundle's 25% scene-drift threshold. The block-delta property that saves disk is what saves uplink &mdash; same codec mechanic. Note the S-VIDIA platform-wide <strong>up to 60%</strong> claim is for <em>storage</em>; the ~46% figure here is for <em>live uplink</em>. They are related (same codec property) but not interchangeable. Single-camera / single-window sample &mdash; multi-camera follow-up implied. See <a href="/docs/benchmarks/05-live-bandwidth-methodology" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">full methodology</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

